WF-31 — Payment Submitted Handler

## Summary

- Purpose: Thin state handler for `payment_submitted` user text. Two parallel branches: Branch A classifies via WF-25 and replies (Gemini contextual reply for general enquiry, canned "under review" reassurance otherwise); Branch B unconditionally relays every inbound message into the user's consult Slack channel (tagged with time-since-paid). stop_intent needs no Branch-A extra (WF-25 sent the clarifier); garbage / abuse terminate inside WF-25.
- Inputs (WF-01 canonical envelope §2.1): `phoneNumber` (top-level), `messageContent`, `user.{id, name, status, slack_channel_id}`, plus `messageText`, `userId`, `userStatus`. `user.slack_channel_id` drives the Branch-B relay (no DB re-fetch).
- Outputs: Branch A — a Gemini reply or canned "under review" reassurance via WF-50. Branch B — a Slack relay of the user message into the consult channel (always).
- State Transitions: none.
- Calls Sub-Workflows: WF-25 (Intent Classifier + Safety-Net Hub), WF-53 (U1 — on the local Gemini reply's failure), WF-50 (Send WhatsApp), WF-51 (Send Slack — Branch B relay).
- **Deltas vs the prior WF-31 (safety-net §6):**
  - REMOVED the inline Gemini-error halt-and-notify chain → on Branch-A Gemini failure, call U1.
  - REMOVED the in-handler stop_intent clarifier (now in WF-25).
  - Branch B (unconditional Slack relay) is UNCHANGED — it relays every inbound (incl. stop_intent / garbage), independent of Branch A.
- **Notes:**
  - Branches A and B run in parallel from the trigger; Branch B fires regardless of intent (and regardless of any Branch-A halt).
  - Copy reuse-existing — verify verbatim at build.

---

## Algorithm

Step 1: Start — triggered by WF-02 with the WF-01 canonical envelope plus `{ messageText, userId, userStatus }`. Read `phoneNumber` and `user.slack_channel_id` from the envelope.
Step 2: Fan out in parallel from the trigger: Branch A → Step 3 (intent + reply); Branch B → Step 9 (Slack relay).

(Branch A — user reply)
Step 3: Call WF-25 with `{ phoneNumber, userId, messageContent: messageText, userStatus, userName: user.name, slackChannelId: user.slack_channel_id }`. Receive `intentResult`. (Garbage / abuse / Gemini-failure terminate inside WF-25; control does not return for those.)
Step 4: Check: `intentResult == 'stop_intent'`?
  - If YES → End of Branch A (WF-25 already sent the clarifier; no extra).
  - If NO → go to Step 5.
Step 5: Check: `intentResult == 'general_enquiry'`?
  - If YES → go to Step 6.
  - If NO → go to Step 8.
Step 6: Build a Gemini prompt for a brief, warm reply with the payment-submitted stage cue ("payment is being reviewed by Dr. Chinmay") + an email callout, append the user's message, then POST to Gemini (gemini-2.5-flash-lite, temperature=0.3). On Gemini failure → go to Step 7. On success → extract the reply (fallback default), call WF-50 with `{ phoneNumber, messageType: 'text', messageContent: <reply> }`. End of Branch A.
Step 7: Gemini failure — call U1 with `{ phoneNumber, userFacing: true, consultChannelId: user.slack_channel_id, context: { source: 'WF-31', userName: user.name, userStateText: 'payment under review', userMessage: messageContent, errorDetail: <summary> } }`. End of Branch A.
Step 8: Build the canned "under review" reassurance: "⏳ Your payment is currently under review. Chinmay will verify it and get back to you shortly (usually within a few hours). You don't need to do anything else right now. If you have any questions, feel free to ask!" Call WF-50 with `{ phoneNumber, messageType: 'text', messageContent: <message> }`. End of Branch A.

(Branch B — relay user message into the consult Slack channel)
Step 9: SELECT created_at FROM chinmay_astro.payments WHERE user_id = user.id ORDER BY id DESC LIMIT 1 (most recent payment). If no row, treat elapsed as `?`.
Step 10: Compute elapsed-since-paid as a human string: `< 60 min` → "{n} min ago"; `< 24 h` → "{n} h ago"; else "{n} d ago".
Step 11: Build the relay payload: `{ channelId: user.slack_channel_id, messageText: "⏱ Paid {elapsed} · 💬 *Message from {user.name or phoneNumber} (payment under review):*\n>{messageContent}" }`. Call WF-51. End of Branch B.
